  "original_statement": "For d\\ge2, does there exist a real morphism \\phi:\\mathbb{P}^1\\to\\mathbb{P}^1 of degree d with only real periodic points, and does the set of such real morphisms have full dimension, equivalently nonempty interior, in the space of all real degree-d morphisms?",
  "clean_statement": "For $d\\geq2$, let $\\mathcal R_d$ be the set of real morphisms $\\phi:\\mathbb P^1\\to\\mathbb P^1$ of degree $d$ whose periodic points are all real. The existence question has an affirmative answer via Chebyshev maps; does $\\mathcal R_d$ have full dimension, equivalently nonempty interior, in the space of real degree-$d$ morphisms?",
